A note on assets/img/og.jpg
---------------------------

The share image is a rendering of the page itself: it puts the brand logo
(section 2) on top of the CC BY-SA photograph (section 1). Those terms pull in
opposite directions, so the file is offered for reuse under neither. If you
want the photograph, take it from section 1 — those files carry no brand.

This split exists because the background is a licensed photograph. If it is
ever replaced by an image with no attribution requirement, section 1 goes away
and the on-page credit goes with it — see README.md.
